#### Vulnerabilities Identified

* FTP Anonymous Access
* Webmin RCE (CVE-2019-15107)
* WordPress Plugin SQL Injection (CVE-2019-10692)
* Weak WordPress Password (cracked with rockyou.txt)
* Poor security hardening and outdated components. 

#### Conclusion

The assessment achieved full system compromise, including root access, extraction of sensitive credentials, WordPress admin access, and proof of impact through flag retrieval. The report recommends disabling anonymous FTP, patching Webmin and vulnerable plugins, enforcing strong passwords, enabling MFA, restricting unnecessary services, and performing regular vulnerability assessments. 

